{"name":"Bauhaus","hex":"#3f4040","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bauhaus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A modernist style characterized by the absence of ornamentation and by harmony between the function of a building or an object and its design."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bauhaus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bauhaus","blocks":[{"text":"The Staatliches Bauhaus, commonly known as the Bauhaus, was a German art school operational from 1919 to 1933 that combined crafts and the fine arts. The school became famous for its approach to design, which attempted to unify individual artistic vision with the principles of mass production and emphasis on function."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/6265_Dessau.JPG/330px-6265_Dessau.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bauhaus","wikidata":"Q124354"},{"title":"Bauhaus (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Bauhaus were an English rock band formed in Northampton in 1978. Known for their dark image and gloomy sound, Bauhaus are one of the pioneers of gothic rock, although they mixed many genres, including dub, glam rock, psychedelia, and funk. The group consisted of Daniel Ash, Peter Murphy, Kevin Haskins (drums) and David J (bass)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Bauhaus_August_2006_UK.jpg/330px-Bauhaus_August_2006_UK.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bauhaus_(band)","wikidata":"Q180582"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/BauhausType.jpg/500px-BauhausType.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/BauhausType.jpg/1280px-BauhausType.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/BauhausType.jpg/500px-BauhausType.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Typography by Herbert Bayer above the entrance to the workshop block of the Bauhaus Dessau, 2005","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABauhausType.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/WalterGropius-1919.jpg/500px-WalterGropius-1919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/WalterGropius-1919.jpg/500px-WalterGropius-1919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bauhaus founder Walter Gropius (1883–1969)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWalterGropius-1919.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Joost_Schmidt_Bauhausausstellung_1923.jpg/330px-Joost_Schmidt_Bauhausausstellung_1923.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Joost_Schmidt_Bauhausausstellung_1923.jpg/330px-Joost_Schmidt_Bauhausausstellung_1923.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poster for the Bauhausausstellung (1923)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoost_Schmidt_Bauhausausstellung_1923.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Bauhaus_weimar.jpg/500px-Bauhaus_weimar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Bauhaus_weimar.jpg/500px-Bauhaus_weimar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The main building of the Bauhaus-University Weimar. Built between 1904 and 1911 and designed by Henry van de Velde to house the sculptors' studio at the Grand Ducal Saxon Art School, it was designated a UNESCO 